(A thing's list field is an owning place like a variable: passed as two
 parameters it is one list under both, grown and freed through either. A
 thing parameter is a copy of the caller's thing, so what the function does
 to its fields stays in the copy.)
A thing called note has
  a list called tags,
  a buffer called body.

To 'merge' of a list called first and a list called second.
    For each number from 1 to 20, append the number to first.
    Print "second sees: {second's length}".
    Free first.
    Print "second now: {second's length}".

To 'keep' with a note called kept.
    'merge' of kept's tags and kept's tags.
    Print "kept: {kept's tags's length}".

a note called memo.
'merge' of memo's tags and memo's tags.
Print "memo: {memo's tags's length}".
a note called other.
append "z" to other's tags.
'keep' of other.
Print "other: {other's tags's length}".
